1
00:00:38,571 --> 00:00:44,571
New adventure. Same wingman.

2
00:01:17,142 --> 00:01:23,142
Carl's Date is a animation, family, comedy film directed by Bob Peterson.

3
00:01:55,714 --> 00:02:01,714
Carl Fredricksen reluctantly agrees to go on a date with a lady
friend—but admittedly has no idea how dating works these days.

4
00:02:34,285 --> 00:02:40,285
Ever the helpful friend, Dug steps in to calm Carl's pre-date jitters and offer
some tried-and-true tips for making friends—if you're a dog.

5
00:03:12,857 --> 00:03:18,857
Carl (voice), played by Ed Asner.

6
00:03:51,428 --> 00:03:57,428
Dug / Alpha (voice), played by Bob Peterson.

7
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Carl's Date (also known as Dug Days: Carl's Date) is a 2023 American animated short film produced by
Pixar Animation Studios, written and directed by Bob Peterson and produced by Kim Collins.

8
00:05:08,571 --> 00:05:14,571
It acts as the sixth and final episode of the miniseries Dug Days,
as well as the final entry in the Up franchise.

9
00:05:47,142 --> 00:05:53,142
It stars the voice of Ed Asner, in his final acting role
before his death in 2021, and Peterson.

10
00:06:25,714 --> 00:06:31,714
The short film follows Carl Fredricksen (Asner), who reluctantly goes on his first date
since his late wife Ellie's death, but has no idea how dating works.

11
00:07:04,285 --> 00:07:10,285
Originally planned for release on Disney+, Carl's Date premiered in
theaters on June 16, 2023, along with Pixar's Elemental.

12
00:07:42,857 --> 00:07:48,857
The film explores themes of date, love, dog, short film.

13
00:08:21,428 --> 00:08:27,428
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
